s like few we've seen in  the series  it's a big sad for sure  and to be honest i could talk about cute  things like that all day but to hell  with all that because the implications  of this chapter's ending  is something groundbreaking and it  involves  the big chair all right so we understand  the hierarchy of the world government  right we have the kings of the various  countries and lands we have the  celestial dragons and we have the five  elders above that  during this arc thanks to our favorite  blind boy steli we understand that there  was a throne to never be sat on that  effectively worked as the throne for the  king of the world  this is when we hear chatter from the  five elders discussing how the nefertari  family dynasty are traitors to their way  after choosing to remain in the lower  realm this  is vivi's family however something more  pressing is worrying them with it only  being two years removed from the  paramount war and with the talks between  kaido and big mom  evident for all to hear they are worried  that they cannot maintain the world's  equilibrium forever and that the time  has come  for a great cleansing i have  no idea what that means really but i can  speculate however before i do  this tall shadowy boy is the great emu  emu or so he's called strewn across the  floor are tattered images of luffy  blackbeard and shirahoshi combination of  wanted posters and regular photographs  they are  all massively important individuals  within the world and  one that's missing i think to me is momo  with his power to communicate to the  massive elephant of zou  which makes sense as wano is perhaps an  unknown to the wider world however  what's interesting is that in his hand  is a photograph of princess vivi  as he scales the steps towards the  throne that no one is to be sat upon  the five elders then bow and ask if  another light is to be erased from  history  the only glimpse of his face or her face  we get  is through this panel and in it we see a  very strange  eye now my immediate reaction i will get  to but first i would like to bring to  your attention what my one piece secret  service has brought to my attention  first  firstly what's interesting and  immediately striking about this  individual is his eye  obviously so where have we seen an eye  like this before  well two places have been brought to my  attention mihawk  and the great elephant of zou somehow i  don't think either of them are beneath  that cloak but what it might be  indicative of is a deeper mastery of  hockey seeing as we already associate  that sort of design choice with the eyes  to be associated with hockey mastery in  the first place  with that said it's a tenuous guess  though i would be surprised if these  three entities weren't tied together in  some way shape or form what's more is  that the sword that was stuck  into the ground by the photos i am going  to hazard a guess as to the significance  of it it's been said through  conversations with steli that the  weapons dotted around the throne were  put there by the 20 that established the  world government  20 weapons now i've gone back over the  images of this throne but i can't get a  good  view of the weapons put into the floor  but no image shows all 20 weapons one  thing for certain though is that i  cannot see  all 20. in addition this emu guy is tied  with the responsibility of the void  century which  means that sword planted in the ground  which he was using could very well  be his own with the tattered ruin he's  left blackbeard and luffy's posters in  it's clear he's been aware of them for  quite some time and has been troubled by  their exploits made evident by their  tattered remains  shirahoshi however has more recently  come to his attention and has also been  recently stabbed since her utility has  just become known as i've said momo  still isn't widely known yet and  furthermore vivi's in the perfect  condition and in his possession  meaning her importance is clear but in a  way that is yet unknown to us  he could very well be a great ancestor  of hers i mean we do know the bloodline  she represents is important  and it was mentioned at the end of that  chapter yet again however that makes me  feel like it's a misdirection and she  might be required for a different reason  additionally something that was brought  to my attention is that the op-op fruit  may  have been used to prolong this emu  individual's life  it's been explained to us already that  the ultimate power of the apa fruit is  to grant someone eternal life in  exchange for the wielder's own life  so i wouldn't be surprised if this is  that man but  overall i don't think we have the means  with which to derive a conclusion just  yet  just a bunch of ill-refined theories but  it's interesting to say the least  or at least i don't i mean it could have  something to do with why the zoe  elephant is walking forever or where  it's walking too  it's a mystery and bizarre to say the  least and that's not even to make  mention of the poneglyphs and raftel on  a narrative first  impressions level i do have my own  thoughts on the utility of this reveal  and how it conflicts with my  expectations  from the outset these are not complaints  or disappointments just my internal  thoughts as i discovered this new entity  from about alabasta until now i sort of  assume the ultimate roadblock at the end  of this  journey for luffy would not be a person  but a concept an idea  a culture or sociological structure  usually in the real world  no one person is to blame for the  world's issues and that's what makes  solving global issues difficult  everyone has a different point of view  there's nuance and throughout this story  luffy whenever he's needed to solve a  problem is very  much a hammer in search of a nail and  he's tremendously effective as a hammer  don't get me wrong but it's the quiet  moments with luffy as he tries to  communicate with his crew  to work on a problem or with other  people where he tries to solve their  problems  using his emotional maturity is what i  always found to be the most interesting  aspect of his character and seeing as  luffy's solution is to typically  punch the bad guy in any given arc i was  sort of anticipating luffy's struggle in  grappling with and being confronted by a  more nuanced and complicated problem  than simply punching a person could  solve  seeing as up until this point there's  been no one person to blame for the  world's issues and even if there was you  would think they would be long since  deceased  however now there seems to be someone to  blame for everything and therefore a  problem that once again in theory  luffy can rectify with the right punch  maybe  i don't know it's a possibility now with  all of that said this is an amazing  story and i am in no way insinuating  that there will be no complexity  if anything this video has communicated  i believe it will be very complex  i was just sort of anticipating a  different sort of big bad if that is in  fact what he  is to take a different more nuanced form  to reflect the complexities odis painted  his world to have  rather than making it a much more  straightforward situation that being  to just take the guy out now in saying  that i appreciate how giving the  audience a goal is great  but again it seems sort of late to be  revealing this big bad  but who knows maybe he's been working  behind the scenes and we've known about  him since the very beginning that's  totally a very odor thing to do  maybe it was the mayor of windmill  village he's never supported luffy's  efforts  jokes aside though i believe there will  be plenty of complexity and nuance as  this story marches on in its final  stretch  with the navy showing some doubt in  various forces around the world  including the celestial dragons  demonstrating that they can be reasoned  with it's going  to be a very interesting and nuanced  story and that's for certain  [Music]  in conclusion when i started this series  i knew it was going to be tough i knew  that there was a reason not many  channels just pick up and review this  the way that i have and  last week i think i hit that wall for  the very first time which is why for one  i will be reviewing the axe individually  hopefully with these smaller chunks i'll  be able to dive into greater detail with  the wonderful story oda has written for  us  with that said that'll do it for today's  video i'll see you all next week when we  finally get to wano and thank you so  much for watching and thank you so much  for your patience  [Music]  you
 

